      <guid isPermaLink="false">d43f8d0871c3e17f70d9c284</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:43:36 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Berlin, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

Nvidia’s board has been working with an outside firm to identify potential replacements for Chief Executive Officer Jensen Huang following reports of multiple extramarital affairs, including one with a woman who is reportedly suspected of spying for China, a person familiar with the situation said.

And Xi Jinping’s third summit of the year with Donald Trump is going off script before their meetings even get underway, as the spy allegations engulfing Nvidia’s Jensen Huang reopen old rifts.

Today's guest: Roland Busch, Siemens, CEO. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
